<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0234">Remark <span data-tag="0234">4.3.3.23</span>.</a> Let $X$, $Y$, and $K$ be simplicial sets. Unwinding the definitions, we see that morphisms from $K$ to $X \star Y$ can be identified with triples $(\pi , f_{-}, f_{+} )$, where </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \pi : K \rightarrow \Delta ^1 \quad \quad f_{-}: \{ 0\}  \times _{\Delta ^1} K \rightarrow X \quad \quad f_{+}: \{ 1\}  \times _{\Delta ^1} K \rightarrow Y \]
</div>
<p> are morphisms of simplicial sets (note that, when $K$ is a simplex, this recovers the description of Remark <a data-tag="0172" href="/tag/0172">4.3.3.19</a>). </p>
</article>
